codex
The failure is reproducible from the state model: `PhasePreparing` currently records only the final desired digest, so a valid interrupted prefix is indistinguishable from foreign bytes. I’m implementing a durable preparation manifest and progress cursor: each filesystem entry is declared before creation, completed entries are digest-checked, and only the active file may be a verified prefix of the recorded source. Recovery will reject unrecorded additions or changed entries before removing anything.
